Starting from the definitions of the ladder operators, we expand \(\hat{a}\hat{a}^{\dagger}\):
\[
\hat{a}\hat{a}^{\dagger}
=
\frac{m\omega}{2\hbar}
\left(\hat{x} + \frac{i}{m\omega}\hat{p}\right)
\left(\hat{x} - \frac{i}{m\omega}\hat{p}\right).
\]

Multiplying out the brackets gives
\[
\hat{a}\hat{a}^{\dagger}
=
\frac{m\omega}{2\hbar}
\left(
\hat{x}^{2}
-
\frac{i}{m\omega}\hat{x}\hat{p}
+
\frac{i}{m\omega}\hat{p}\hat{x}
+
\frac{1}{m^{2}\omega^{2}}\hat{p}^{2}
\right).
\]

Similarly, for \(\hat{a}^{\dagger}\hat{a}\) we obtain
\[
\hat{a}^{\dagger}\hat{a}
=
\frac{m\omega}{2\hbar}
\left(\hat{x} - \frac{i}{m\omega}\hat{p}\right)
\left(\hat{x} + \frac{i}{m\omega}\hat{p}\right).
\]

Expanding gives
\[
\hat{a}^{\dagger}\hat{a}
=
\frac{m\omega}{2\hbar}
\left(
\hat{x}^{2}
+
\frac{i}{m\omega}\hat{x}\hat{p}
-
\frac{i}{m\omega}\hat{p}\hat{x}
+
\frac{1}{m^{2}\omega^{2}}\hat{p}^{2}
\right).
\]

Now subtract the two expressions:
\[
\hat{a}\hat{a}^{\dagger} - \hat{a}^{\dagger}\hat{a}
=
\frac{m\omega}{2\hbar}
\left(
-
\frac{2i}{m\omega}\hat{x}\hat{p}
+
\frac{2i}{m\omega}\hat{p}\hat{x}
\right).
\]

Factoring out the common coefficient gives
\[
\hat{a}\hat{a}^{\dagger} - \hat{a}^{\dagger}\hat{a}
=
\frac{i}{\hbar}
\left(
\hat{p}\hat{x} - \hat{x}\hat{p}
\right).
\]

Hence,
\[
\hat{a}\hat{a}^{\dagger} - \hat{a}^{\dagger}\hat{a}
=
\frac{i}{\hbar}\left(\hat{p}\hat{x} - \hat{x}\hat{p}\right).
\]

